================================================================================
Language, runtime, and redistributed libraries
================================================================================

Mojo and the Modular runtime — Modular Inc. (https://www.modular.com)
Pion is written in Mojo. A prebuilt Pion binary or container image is
statically linked against, and redistributes in object form, the Modular
runtime libraries (libKGENCompilerRTShared, libAsyncRTRuntimeGlobals,
libMSupportGlobals). Those libraries are proprietary to Modular Inc. and are
redistributed under the Modular Community License
(https://www.modular.com/legal/community); all rights in them are reserved by
Modular Inc. Building Pion from source obtains them through the Modular
toolchain and redistributes nothing.


================================================================================
Wire-protocol compatibility (no code from these projects is included)
================================================================================

Redis — Redis Ltd. (https://redis.io)
Valkey — the Valkey project, a Linux Foundation project (https://valkey.io)
Pion implements the RESP2/RESP3 wire protocol for client compatibility with
Redis and Valkey. Pion is an independent implementation and is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Redis Ltd. or the Valkey project.


================================================================================
Acknowledgements
================================================================================

Pion's design draws on published research and interoperates with a number of
open-source projects. None of the following contributes code to Pion; they are
acknowledged here for their ideas or as integration targets:

  HNSW — Malkov & Yashunin, "Efficient and Robust Approximate Nearest
    Neighbor Search using Hierarchical Navigable Small World Graphs" (2016):
    the approximate-nearest-neighbor algorithm behind Pion's vector search.
  The training-free sparse-attention and quantization literature that informs
    Pion's sparse-mask attention and INT4/INT3/INT2 vector compression.
  vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) and LMCache
    (https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache): interface targets for externalized
    attention and KV-cache tensor storage.
  mlx-lm — Apple / MLX contributors (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm):
    the Apple Silicon inference library the pion-vllm-mlx consumer integrates
    with. Apache-2.0.
  Ollama (https://ollama.com): a local embedding/LLM provider Pion can use.
  Superlinked SIE (https://github.com/superlinked/sie): an optional embedding
    and reranking backend. Apache-2.0.
  oMLX (https://github.com/jundot/omlx): a Mac-native inference server whose
    tiered KV-cache persistence informed Pion's SSD-tier design. Apache-2.0.
  Sentence-Transformers / all-MiniLM-L6-v2 — the default auto-embed model.
  LangChain / LangGraph, AutoGen (Microsoft), LlamaIndex: frameworks for which
    Pion ships integration packages.
  memtier_benchmark (Redis Ltd.) and VectorDBBench (Zilliz Inc.): benchmark
    harnesses used to measure Pion.


